 "script": {
  "hook": "One network call per tap drains the battery. Batch your events instead.",
  "question": "Design event batching and flushing.",
  "trap": "The trap: send every event the moment it happens. It wakes the radio, burns battery, and loses events on a crash.",
  "steps": [
   "Buffer. Append each event to a small queue, and write it to disk. Never one request per event.",
   "Flush triggers. Flush on batch size, on a timer, and when the app goes to background. Whichever comes first.",
   "Send. Compress the batch and give it an id. Retry with backoff, and the server drops duplicates.",
   "Delete late. Remove events from disk only after the server confirms. A crash then loses nothing."
  ],
  "takeaway": "Buffer on disk, flush on triggers, delete only after the confirm.",
  "teaser": "Tomorrow: the offline event queue.",
  "cta": "Comment M S D for the free cheatsheet."
 },
